# This worktree is checked out on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, but the
# build and every experiment run under WSL. A shell script checked out with
# CRLF is not merely ugly: bash fails on the trailing $'\r' of every line,
# and a gate driver that had been rewritten with CRLF once already turned a
# whole matrix run into a no-op that reported success per step
# (docs/phase0-phase1-report.md, section 2.10). Pin the line endings of
# everything an interpreter reads directly.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
